# HomeKit Services Implementation Verification

## Overview
This rule defines the requirements for implementing HomeKit services in the OpenHAB HomeKit binding.

## Author
Karel Goderis

## Requirements

### 0. Source Information
Cross-reference with the file [ServiceDefinitions.ts](mdc:https:/raw.githubusercontent.com/homebridge/HAP-NodeJS/refs/heads/latest/src/lib/definitions/ServiceDefinitions.ts)
Every file verified needs to be "saved" so that its last modified date gets updated

### 1. Base Class Selection
- All services must extend `AbstractHomekitService`
- Place in `src/main/java/org/openhab/io/homekit/library/service/`
- Annotate with `@HomekitServiceType` including:
  - `type`: UUID from HAP specification
  - `name`: Name from HAP specification
  - `tag`: camelCase version of name

### 2. Class Structure
- Implement required characteristics as defined in ServiceDefinitions.ts
- Add optional characteristics if needed
- Use proper null safety annotations (`@NonNullByDefault`)
- Follow Java naming conventions
- Import all necessary classes and do not use fully qualified classnames
- Use with() methods in constructors
- Cross-check the UUID and name with what is in ServiceDefinitions.ts
- Remove @override methods that are redundant
- Every file verified needs to be "saved" so that its last modified date gets updated
- Add mandatory characteristics, and use withMandatory(true)
- Add optional characteristics, and use withMandatory(false)

### 3. Documentation
- Add Javadoc comment referencing the HAP specification in general to https://developer.apple.com/documentation/HomeKit (do not use a specific or non-existing url)
- Remove any references to homebridge.io
- Include service description and purpose
- Include an author field : "Karel Goderis"
- Include documentation for each method

### 4. Code Quality
- Remove unnecessary `@Override` methods that only call `super()`
- Use proper null safety annotations (`@NonNullByDefault`)
- Follow Java naming conventions
- Import all necessary classes and do not use fully qualified classnames
- Replace full qualified classes like java.util.Map with Map, or java.util.Collections and so forth, and add an import line

### 5. Service Configuration
- Set required characteristics as per HAP specification
- Add optional characteristics if needed
- Configure service properties (isHidden, isPrimary, isExtensible) appropriately
- Handle characteristic initialization in initialise() method

## Example Implementation
```java
/**
 * HomeKit Service Name.
 * This service represents [description].
 *
 * @author Karel Goderis
 */
@HomekitServiceType(type = "UUID", name = "Name", tag = "camelCaseName")
@NonNullByDefault
public class HomekitServiceName extends AbstractHomekitService {
    public HomekitServiceName(HomekitAccessory accessory, HomekitEventManager eventManager,
            HomekitCharacteristicFactory characteristicFactory) {
        super(accessory, eventManager, characteristicFactory);
        withName("Service Name")
            .withExtensible(true)
            .withPrimary(false)
            .withHidden(false);
    }

    @Override
    public void addCharacteristics() {
        // Add required characteristics
        addCharacteristic(new HomekitRequiredCharacteristic(this, eventManager, 
            getAccessory().getNextAvailableInstanceId()));
        
        // Add optional characteristics if needed
        addCharacteristic(new HomekitOptionalCharacteristic(this, eventManager,
            getAccessory().getNextAvailableInstanceId()));
    }
}
```

